From c4b30c44dcf83944a24d9a87150bfe2030284e53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:47:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] openssl: build with OpenSSL 4.1

OpenSSL 4.1 deprecates X509_check_host() and X509_check_ip_asc(), in
favour of setting the reference identity with
X509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_host() before the handshake, and the build, which
turns warnings into errors, stops on the two calls.

Silence the deprecation warning for these two calls only. The check is
the one OpenSSL 4.1 makes: since 4.1 the subject commonName of a
certificate without a DNS subject alternative name is no longer matched
(nor constrained by the name constraints of its issuers), so a server
certificate with only a commonName does not pass the host name check,
which the connector makes for servers that are not on a local address
(send_client_reply_packet() in plugins/auth/my_auth.c). Moving to the
X509_VERIFY_PARAM path would change when and how the connector reports a
verification failure; that is for upstream to decide.
---
 libmariadb/secure/openssl.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libmariadb/secure/openssl.c b/libmariadb/secure/openssl.c
index 7b45625..2d75161 100644
--- a/libmariadb/secure/openssl.c
+++ b/libmariadb/secure/openssl.c
@@ -883,12 +883,23 @@ int ma_tls_verify_server_cert(MARIADB_TLS *ctls, unsigned int verify_flags)
     }
 
   #ifdef HAVE_OPENSSL_CHECK_HOST
+    /*
+      Deprecated in OpenSSL 4.1, which wants the reference identity set before
+      the handshake; this check runs after it, and the functions remain.
+    */
+#if defined(__GNUC__)
+#pragma GCC diagnostic push
+#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wdeprecated-declarations"
+#endif
     if (X509_check_host(cert, mysql->host, strlen(mysql->host), 0, 0) != 1
        && X509_check_ip_asc(cert, mysql->host, 0) != 1)
     {
       mysql->net.tls_verify_status|= MARIADB_TLS_VERIFY_HOST;
       goto error;
     }
+#if defined(__GNUC__)
+#pragma GCC diagnostic pop
+#endif
   #else
     x509sn= X509_get_subject_name(cert);
 
-- 
2.53.0

